From cc80f2b34070de28a52ae1a0810aed088607fadc Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 12:50:20 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] [daveey] desktop: sidebar background dot reads all its
 stores, falls back to the listed row, says "waiting"

Follow-ups from the PR #2154 review (review 5890296461):

1. Tick lag. `useBackgroundDotUnknown` and `useSessionDotState` subscribed only to
   `$kanbanObservationTick` (plus the id stores), while `rowExecution` also reads
   `$liveWorkRoster`, `$backgroundStatusBySession`, `$subagentsBySession`,
   `$sessionStates` and `$sessions`. A roster or event change that flipped `exec.live`
   repainted the label/state only on the next 15 s tick. Both hooks now use
   `useStoresSelector` over every read store (`ROW_EXECUTION_STORES`). `$sessionStates`
   is reduced to a computed runtime->stored-id key so per-token republishes do not
   re-run the selector.
2. Null row. A dot with no caller row (contrib tab lead, unresolved `tileStoredRow`)
   evaluated `{}` and said "status unknown" for a store-claimed `background_active` /
   `goal_active`. It now falls back to the listed `$sessions` / `$messagingSessions`
   row by id.
3. Waiting label. `backgroundDotUnknown` becomes `backgroundDotLabel` ->
   `running | unknown | waiting`. A fresh row held only by known waiting work (all
   cards parked/held or current waiting observations; no unparked, blocked, needs-you
   or outstanding ask) reads "Open work, waiting" (new `sidebar.row.backgroundWaiting`
   in all 8 locales + _keys.desktop.json).

Tests: session-status-dot.test.tsx (new, component-level RED on base for all three
points) and session-dot-state.test.ts backgroundDotLabel cases.
